# Collision-induced absorption (CIA) tables.
# Generated by tools/build_cia_table.py -- see that file for
# full provenance, unit and convention notes.  Do not hand-edit.
#
# Stored value is log10 of the binary absorption coefficient in
# cm^5:  kappa [cm^2/g] = 10**value * n_1 * n_2 / rho,  with n in
# cm^-3.  STIMULATED EMISSION IS ALREADY INCLUDED -- the consuming
# code must not apply a (1 - exp(-h nu / kT)) factor to these.
#
# Sources:
#   H2-H2  Abel, Frommhold, Li & Hunt 2011, J.Phys.Chem.A 115, 6805 [+ Borysow, Jorgensen & Fu 2001 continuation]
#   H2-He  Abel, Frommhold, Li & Hunt 2012, J.Phys.Chem.A 116, 3068
#   H2-H   Gustafsson & Frommhold 2003, A&A 400, 1161
#   H-He   Gustafsson & Frommhold 2001, ApJ 546, 1168
#
# Layout: NPAIR and the largest per-pair temperature count, then
# the shared wavenumber grid (NNU, NU_MIN, D_NU), then per pair:
# name, NTEMP, the temperature list, and NTEMP records of NNU
# values (one record per temperature, ascending nu).  Read
# list-directed.  Below NU_MIN the nu^2 low frequency limit
# applies; above the last point the coefficient is zero.
# Temperatures clamp at both ends.
